course: dictionary
lesson: 1070
title: Boundaries: lines and limits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A boundary is a line that marks the edge of an area, like a field, a country or a garden. «The usual boundary follows the Ural Mountains, the Ural River, the Caspian Sea» shows a line drawn to mark where one area ends and another begins.
explain: The same word also works in games and in life. In cricket, the boundary is the edge of the field, and hitting the ball over it scores runs. Boundaries can also be limits on what is OK to do. «Boundaries are limits you set for yourself» means rules about what you will and won't allow.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. If the sentence talks about a map, a field or a country, boundary means an edge or line. If it talks about being safe, being fair, or saying no, boundary means a limit. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «a limit you set» fit? Then it is the right one.
fact: A boundary is a line or edge that marks where an area ends.
fact: In cricket, hitting the ball over the boundary scores 4 or 6 runs.
fact: Boundaries can also be limits on what is OK to do, such as personal boundaries.
fact: «Testing boundaries» means misbehaving on purpose to see what is allowed.
fact: A boundary between countries is the line where one country ends and the next begins.
exercise: «A boundary in a shared room has to be fair to both, so both can still reach the door.» What does the boundary have to be? | Only on one person's side of the room | A wall that blocks the door | Hidden under the bed | *Fair to both people, so both can still reach the door
exercise: In cricket, hitting the ball over the boundary scores how many runs? | *4 or 6 runs | No runs at all | 10 runs | 1 or 2 runs
exercise: «Boundaries are limits you set for yourself; after lending £2, £3, £1 and £4, which is £10, and getting £0 back, it is okay to say no and still be friends.» Find and copy one word that means the same as boundaries. | *limits | yourself | lending | friends
test: «Testing boundaries» means misbehaving on purpose to see what is allowed. What does testing boundaries mean? | Keeping every promise you make | *Misbehaving on purpose to see what is allowed | Playing cricket in a big field | Drawing lines on a map of the world
test: Which sentence best describes a boundary between two countries? | A kind of cake made with fruit | A game played with a bat and a ball | *A line that marks where one country ends and the next begins | A tall mountain in the middle of a city
exam: Mia tells her brother, «You must knock before you come into my room; that is my boundary.» What kind of boundary is this? | A map boundary between two countries | A boundary worth six runs | *A personal boundary, a limit on what is OK | A cricket boundary, the edge of a field
